Status: IN PROGRESS
Milestone: Readable side-by-side diagnostics and persistent clean-output access
Dependencies: 16_PREVIEW_FIRST_STUDIO.todo, 19_NUMERIC_CONTROL_CLARITY.todo
Purpose: Follow the user's illustrated settings/preview/stacked-diagnostics layout instead of
  shrinking visual diagnostics into a bottom text drawer.

Tasks:
  [x] Inspect the actual diagnostic widget allocation and clean-window lifecycle.
  [x] Put a readable raw-face panel above face/pose or body diagnostics to the preview's right.
  [x] Reclaim the diagnostic rail when its channels are off; preserve the protected main preview.
  [x] Keep Logs, CLI and numeric signals in Tools rather than squeezing images into it.
  [x] Add a persistent Live-mode action/button to show or reopen clean output after closing it.
  [x] Verify image area, containment, settings access, privacy and real close/reopen behaviour.
  [ ] Update native dark/light README captures, gallery, guide and engineering handbook.
  [ ] Refresh current source/MSI artifacts, commit completed work and offload own context.

Acceptance criteria:
  With the relevant settings enabled, raw face and a tracking diagnostic are simultaneously
  readable beside the main preview without opening Tools. Splitters cannot collapse the
  preview or diagnostic image area. Smaller supported sizes retain the complete preview.
  Flags, raw consent, local-only channels and original output dimensions remain unchanged.
  Closing clean output does not stop the session; a visible Live button reopens the existing
  clean window with current clean pixels. Raw/debug images never appear in that window.
  The front README remains banner/hero, three GIFs and exactly two GUI screenshots; detailed
  screenshots remain in the linked gallery. No camera, portrait or remote publication.

Completion evidence:
  Right-hand raw/face-pose/body rail implemented with independently resizable protected panels.
  Off channels return the full width to the preview; selected channels stay visible with Tools
  closed. No more visual-diagnostic tabs inside the small bottom drawer.
  Native Windows containment/channel/readable-area/primary-action set: 12 passed at each
  100/125/150% Qt scale; Ruff. Covers 1440x810, 1280x720 and 960x600, Tools/errors, actual
  aspect-fitted image area, attempted splitter collapse and Live/Video/headless visibility.
  Compact Tools must have an explicit 1px minimum rather than zero, which retains Qt's 70px
  scroll-area minimum hint. Removed a redundant raw-note row, not privacy/area assertions.
  Show clean output is a persistent Live button sharing the View-menu action. Auto-open is a
  separate preference, not a stale claim that a closed window is still visible. Reopening
  retains the same window and active worker, including when Auto-open is unchecked.
  Idle opening is black and opens no camera; Video/headless/raw configurations cannot display
  a clean window. Closing clean output does not request worker shutdown or change the preference.
  Full suite: 310 passed, one unsupported offscreen-widescreen case skipped; Ruff.
  Final native Windows image/channel/close-reopen/primary-control set: 16 passed at each
  100/125/150% scale. Compact error details shrink within 48-68px and retain full scrollable text
  instead of forcing the protected image panels outside their parents.
  Final screenshot/docs/snapshot verification is still pending.
  User usability approval remains separate from automated/synthetic evidence.

Completion log:
  2026-11-03: User rejected the tiny raw-face strip and supplied a concrete illustration:
  move the main preview beside the settings edge and use the freed right column for two
  stacked diagnostics. Also requested an always-accessible clean-output reopen button and
  refreshed README. No additional design questionnaire or unrelated research is needed.
